<title>USA: Daisytek International Corp Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>Daisytek International Corp Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						   Sept. 30,</p>
<p>						1996     1995  % Change</p>
<p> Net sales			    $138,148 $105,421    31.0%</p>
<p> Cost of sales			 124,559   94,086    32.4%</p>
<p>    Gross profit			13,589   11,335    19.9%</p>
<p> SG&amp;A expenses			   8,397    6,685    25.6%</p>
<p>    Income from operations	   5,192    4,650    11.7%</p>
<p> Interest expense			  413	417   (1.0)%</p>
<p>    Income before income taxes     4,779    4,233    12.9%</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	  1,824    1,617    12.8%</p>
<p> Net income				2,955    2,616    13.0%</p>
<p> Net income per common share	  0.43     0.39(a) 10.3%</p>
<p> Weighted avg shares outstanding   6,921    6,733</p>
<p>						  Six Months</p>
<p> Net sales			    $275,042 $210,387    30.7%</p>
<p> Cost of sales			 247,783  188,418    31.5%</p>
<p>    Gross Profit			27,259   21,969    24.1%</p>
<p> SG&amp;A expenses			  16,703   13,280    25.8%</p>
<p>    Income from operations	  10,556    8,689    21.5%</p>
<p> Interest expense			  845	766    10.3%</p>
<p>    Income before income taxes     9,711    7,923    22.6%</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes	  3,715    3,039    22.2%</p>
<p> Net income				5,996    4,884    22.8%</p>
<p> Net income per common share	  0.87     0.73(a) 19.2%</p>
<p> Weighted avg shares outstanding   6,915    6,731</p>
<p>(In Thousands, Except Per Share Data)</p>
<p>NOTE:  (a) Reflects about $.05 per share related to one-time inventory purchase actions.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
